sermo (modular edition), List of authors and contributors
==========================================================

Project: sermo — modular edition (libsermocore core + rendering backends)
Site   : https://haplo-dialog.fr
Email  : devel@haplo-dialog.fr

──────────────────────────────────────────────────
Main author
──────────────────────────────────────────────────

S. Cage — haplo-dialog <devel@haplo-dialog.fr>
  - libsermocore core (parsing + hardened execution, no toolkit)
  - Nine rendering backends: gtk3, gtk4, qt6, fltk1, efl1, sdl3, lvgl, ncurses, html
  - Separate packaging, core↔backend boundary contract

──────────────────────────────────────────────────
sermo lineage
──────────────────────────────────────────────────

The modular edition continues the sermo lineage (43+ widgets, safe_system
hardening, output escaping, unified lexer/parser on the gtk3sermo reference).

──────────────────────────────────────────────────
Original upstream, gtkdialog
──────────────────────────────────────────────────

sermo is a fork of gtkdialog. Upstream copyright notices are kept in every file
that descends from it (see LICENCES.en.md).

Pere László <pipas@linux.pte.hu>
  - Original author of gtkdialog (copyright 2003-2007)

Thunor <thunorsif@hotmail.com>
  - Second maintainer of gtkdialog, 2011-2013: 0.8.x series, up to 0.8.3
    (copyright 2011-2012)

Kiss Gábor <gabor@gamma.ttk.pte.hu>
  - gtkdialog documentation

gtkdialog patches (from its AUTHORS file):
  Moose On The Loose <kensmith1313666@gmail.com>, Patriot,
  Fabio Tranchitella <kobold@debian.org>, Luca Falavigna <dktrkranz@ubuntu.com>,
  Szabo Viktor <wyck@freemail.hu>, Csaszar-Csutoras Peter <spy@c2.hu>

──────────────────────────────────────────────────
Wayland anchoring (layer-shell), woof-CE / Puppy Linux line
──────────────────────────────────────────────────

Written in gtkdialog at woof-CE, then carried into gtk3dialog (01micko),
which BunsenLabs packages; sermo ported it from the latter. Full history:
HISTOIRE.en.md.

Dima Krasner <dima@dimakrasner.com>
  - Wayland layer-shell anchoring in woof-CE gtkdialog (2021)

Mick Amadio (01micko) <01micko@gmail.com>
  - Wayland layer-shell anchoring, continued (2021-2024); author of gtk3dialog

